And yet somehow that volcanic eruption leaves actual blight on the island.

[/quote]

Interesting point -- if the whole thing is just a nightmare about a volcano destroying the island, how does it produce "fictitious" damage, but "real" blight?&nbsp;

It seems like you can't have it both ways -- if BODAN's powers can't do any physical damage to things, they shouldn't be able to do any physical blight, either.&nbsp; And really, they shouldn't be able to *remove* blight, either.&nbsp; A beautiful dream that the island has been cleaned up doesn't mean that the island has in fact actually *been* cleaned up.

And what about the Dahan?&nbsp; A power like (ex:) Razor Sharp Undergrowth or Poisoned Land is supposed to destroy Dahan.&nbsp; The card says "...nor can [your Powers] destroy anything except your own [Presence]," which seems to indicate that those powers would not, in fact, destroy any Dahan.&nbsp; What do they in fact, do?&nbsp; The "destroyed" explorers/towns move elsewhere, but do the "destroyed" Dahan just stay where they are?&nbsp;&nbsp;

(Apologies, BTW, if these issues/questions have been addressed in other FAQs/threads.)

